<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang='en-US'><head><meta content="text/html; charset=UTF-8" http-equiv="Content-Type"/><script>window['ec:pageId']='11183348780403914911'</script><title>CFP</title><link href="/images/favicon.ico" rel="icon" type="image/jpeg"/><link href="/css/cool.css?version=545" rel="StyleSheet" type="text/css"/>
<link href="/css/cfp/classic.css?version=545" rel="StyleSheet" type="text/css"/>
<link href="/css/menu_cfp.css?version=545" rel="StyleSheet" type="text/css"/>
<script src="/js/easy.js?version=545"></script><script src="/js/menu.js?version=545"></script><script src="/js/form.js?version=545"></script><script src="/js/inplace.js?version=545"></script><script>EC.version='545'</script></head>
<body><table class="page" id="page"><tr style="height:1px"><td><table class="header"><tr><td class="logocell"><a href="/" title="EasyChair home page"><img class="leftlogo" src="/images/logoEC_short.png"/></a></td><td class="rolecell">EasyChair Smart CFP</td><td style="width: 99%"></td><td class="helplink"><a class="toplinks" href="/docs/home" title="User guide">User guide</a></td></tr></table></td></tr><tr style="height:99%"><td class="menu_and_content"><div class="menu" id="menu0"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="menu" style="position:static; visibility:visible"><tr><td class="top" id="menu1" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu1','/cfp',{&quot;a&quot;:null})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu1')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu1')" title="Main page">Home</td><td class="top" id="menu2" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu2','/cfp/choose',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu2')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu2')" title="Create a new CFP">New CFP</td><td class="top" id="menu3" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu3','/cfp/all',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu3')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu3')" title="Manage my CFPs">My CFPs</td><td class="top" id="menu4" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu4','/cfp/watchlist',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu4')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu4')" title="My CFP watchlist">Watchlist</td></tr></table></div><div class="search_row" id="cfp:search:row"><form action="/cfp/search" id="search-form"><input id="search-input" name="query" placeholder="Search" type="text"/></form></div><div class="summary"><div class="pagetitle">CFP</div></div><div class="content" id="content"><div class="subcontent"><div id="cfp" style="clear:right"><table class="title_table"><tr><td class="logocell"><img src="/images/cfp-logo/EDT2027.jpg?id=2090566556"/></td><td class="titlecell"><div id="cfptitle">EDT 2027: The International Scientific Conference "Emerging and Disruptive Technologies’ Impact on Global Security"</div><div id="cfpvenue">"Nicolae Balcescu" Land Forces Academy, Revolutiei Street no. 3-5</div><div id="cfpdateplace">Sibiu, Romania, March 26, 2027</div></td></tr></table><table class="date_table"><tr><td>Conference web page</td><td><a href="https://www.armyacademy.ro/engleza/conference_EDT.php" target="_blank">https://www.armyacademy.ro/engleza/conference_EDT.php</a></td></tr><tr><td>Submission link</td><td><a href="https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=edt2027" target="_blank">https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=edt2027</a></td></tr><tr><td>Submission deadline</td><td>January 22, 2027</td></tr></table><div class="topics">Topics: <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=44425585" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_navy bg_darkyellow">technical and systemic perspectives</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=44425586" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_fuchsia bg_yellow">operational perspectives in d&amp;s</span></a></div><p>The EDT 2027 conference, organized by "Nicolae Bălcescu" Land Forces Academy of Sibiu in partnership with the Romanian Academy of Scientists, Technical University of Cluj-Napoca (UTCN), "Titu Maiorescu" University, National Institute for Aerospace Research and Development “Elie Carafoli”, and S. CARFIL S.A., is a place to share and debate new ideas and approaches related to the topic of emerging and disruptive technologies and their impact on global security.</p><h2>Submission Guidelines</h2><p><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif"><span style="font-size:20px">All papers must be original and not simultaneously submitted to another journal or conference and must be edited according to the conference`s template. Papers, written in English,</span></span> <span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif"><span style="font-size:20px">should be submitted via Easy Chair system no later than <strong>January 22, 2027</strong>, describing the aims of the paper, methodology, results and the length of your paper should not be less than 4 pages, or more than 8 pages. Papers must comply with the guidelines described in the KBO Paper format, available </span><span style="font-size:18px">at </span></span><span style="font-size:16px">https://www.armyacademy.ro/engleza/conference_EDT.php .</span></p><h2>List of Topics</h2><p style="margin-left:.5in; mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2; mso-text-indent-alt:-.25in; text-align:justify; text-indent:-.5in"><strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">I.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span></strong><strong>EMERGING AND DISRUPTIVE SOLUTIONS: TECHNICAL AND SYSTEMIC PERSPECTIVES</strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">1.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning in Disruptive Solutions</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">2.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Blockchain and Data Security: Impact and Emerging Applications, from Crypto-Assets to Trusted Infrastructures and Digital Identity</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">3.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">The Role of AI and IoT in Complex Architectures: Challenges and Opportunities in Managing the Resilience of Critical Systems and Services</span></strong><strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"> </strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">4.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Quantum, Edge, and Neuromorphic Computing and Their Disruptive Potential in Complex Systems: Possible Practical Applications and Scaling Challenges in Security, Engineering, and Economics</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">5.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Collaborative Robotics and Interconnected Autonomous Systems</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">6.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Big Data Analytics Mechanisms for System Optimization and Decision-Making, and the Regulation of Rapid Innovation </span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">7.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Civil–Military Cooperation in dual-use Innovation and Technology Transfer</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">8.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Agile Military Communication Architectures and Countermeasures in the Electromagnetic Spectrum</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">9.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Technological Sustainability and Energy Efficiency in Digital Ecosystems</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">10.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">The Strategic Diplomacy of Innovation: Between Technological Progress and Geopolitical Balance</span></strong></p><p style="margin-left:.5in; mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2; mso-text-indent-alt:-.25in; text-align:justify; text-indent:-.5in"><strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">II.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span></strong><strong>EMERGING AND DISRUPTIVE TECHNOLOGIES: OPERATIONAL PERSPECTIVES IN DEFENSE AND SECURITY</strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops:list 42.55pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">1.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Drones and Autonomous Robots in Defense and Security Missions – UAVs, UGVs, USVs, and Swarm Systems; Autonomous Operations in Contested Environments</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops:list 42.55pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">2.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Artificial Intelligence in Cyber Threat Analysis and Prevention, and Real-Time Decision-Making – Autonomous and Semi-Autonomous Command-and-Control (C2) Systems, AI-Based Decision Support and Predictive Analytics in Military Operations</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops:list 42.55pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="letter-spacing:-.2pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">3.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; letter-spacing:-.2pt; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Augmented and Virtual Reality for Military Training and Simulation as Essential Tools for Personnel Preparation and Operational Planning</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops:list 42.55pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">4.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Integration of Uncrewed Platforms into Multi-Domain Operations (Air, Maritime, Land, Space, Cyber, Information)</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops:list 42.55pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">5.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Emerging Technologies in Surveillance and Reconnaissance (Video, Audio, Sensors), Edge Computing, and 6G Networks for Tactical Operations</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops:list 42.55pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">6.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Defensive and Offensive AI in Cyber Operations within the Global Security Environment</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops:list 42.55pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">7.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Innovative Solutions in Transportation and Materials for Enhanced Operational Mobility and Supply Chain Resilience</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops:list 42.55pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">8.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Emerging Technologies for Intelligent Vehicles, Hybrid Propulsion, Ultra-Light Materials, and Resilient Structures for Logistics and Combat Equipment</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops:list 42.55pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">9.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Autonomous Weapons and the Ethics of Digital Warfare: Challenges for International Humanitarian Law</span></strong></p><p style="margin-bottom:0in; margin-left:70.9pt; margin-right:0in; margin-top:0in; mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops:list 42.55pt; text-align:justify; text-indent:-28.35pt"><span style="mso-list:Ignore">10.<span style="font:7.0pt"> </span></span><strong><span style="font-weight:normal; mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Anchoring cyber resilience in a unified digital military system</span></strong></p><h2>Committees</h2><h3>Program Committee - <strong><span lang="RO">CO-CHAIRPERSONS</span></strong></h3><ul><li><strong><span>Dumitru TODOSIUC </span></strong></li><li><strong><span>Teodor FRUNZETI </span></strong></li><li><strong><span>Doina Liana PÎSLĂ </span></strong></li></ul><h3>Organizing Committee<span> - </span><strong><span>CHAIRPERSON</span></strong></h3><ul><li><strong><span>Dorel BADEA</span></strong></li></ul><h2>Invited Speakers - TBA</h2><h2>Publication</h2><p><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,serif; letter-spacing:-0.2pt">Papers presented at the conference will be considered for publication, in a special issue of the ACTA TEHNICA NAPOCENSIS (</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-family:Times New Roman,serif; letter-spacing:-0.2pt"><a href="https://wos-journal.info/journalid/3242">https://wos-journal.info/journalid/3242</a></span><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,serif; letter-spacing:-0.2pt">)</span></span></p><h2>Venue</h2><p>The conference will be held in "Nicolae Balcescu" Land Forces Academy, <span>Revolutiei Street no. 3-5<span><span> Sibiu</span>, <span><span>Romania</span></span></span></span></p><h2>Contact</h2><p>All questions about submissions should be emailed to <span>conference.edt@armyacademy.ro</span></p><h2>Sponsors</h2></div></div></div></td></tr><tr><td class="footer">Copyright © 2002 – 2026 EasyChair</td></tr></table></body></html>
